# The Weather Works: the halyard.
dialogue halyard
  node douse narrator "I pour the lagoon on the great brazier. It dies like an opera singer: hugely, at length, in a great deal of steam."
    -> thins
  node thins narrator "Out on the reef the fog stops being a wall and becomes a rumour. Then it isn't even that. The Needle lies open, blue, as plain as a line on a chart."
    -> men
  node men narrator "Behind us, two men in yellow armbands step out of the smoke. They are smiling. They have cudgels. They wipe their feet."
    -> problem
  node problem weather "Morning. Is there a problem with the weather?"
    > "Yes. I've stopped it." -> stopped
    > "Run, Quill." -> notwithout
      add aff 1
  node stopped weather "Oh dear. Then you'll be needing an inspection. A thorough one."
    -> grab
  node notwithout quill "Not without you."
    -> grab
  node grab narrator "Quill yanks the halyard off its cleat, hooks an arm round my waist and puts one bare foot on the rim of a brazier."
    -> hold
  node hold quill "Hold on to me, cargo."
    > "I am holding on to you." -> keep
      add aff 1
    > "Is this an approved means of—" -> no
  node no quill "No."
    > "I am holding on to you." -> keep
      add aff 1
  node keep quill "Good. Keep doing that."
    -> swing
  node swing narrator "We swing out over the braziers, through the smoke and the heat, and for one long second the whole island is underneath us and none of it is the point."
    go salt_camp
